📘 Agile Scrum MCQs (With Answers)
Q1. Which of the following statements are TRUE with respect to sprint backlog?

A) For sprint backlog creation, user stories are broken down into tasks
B) The sprint backlog cannot be changed once the sprint has started
C) The sprint backlog is a living artifact and is updated on a daily basis
D) Tasks not completed are always moved to next sprint backlog

Answer: ✅ A and C

Q2. A developer cannot proceed due to missing library. What is the correct action?

A) Product Owner resolves it
B) Download free version
C) Assign task to someone else
D) Scrum Master resolves impediment

Answer: ✅ Scrum Master resolves impediment

Q3. Benefits of dividing user stories into tasks

A) Clarifies work
B) Better estimation
C) Enables parallel work
D) Task story points are summed for story

Answer: ✅ A, B and C

Q4. TDD issue despite good coverage

A) Not enough test cases
B) No framework
C) Test cases not reviewed
D) Lack of refactoring

Answer: ✅ Not paid adequate attention to refactoring

Q5. Who decides sprint workload?

A) Scrum Master
B) Product Owner + Scrum Master
C) Product Owner + Team
D) Development Team

Answer: ✅ Development Team

Q6. Best practices for distributed Scrum

A) PO close to client
B) Common Scrum Master for multiple teams
C) Use online tools
D) Respect time zones

Answer: ✅ A, C and D

Q7. Any member can write user stories?

A) True
B) False

Answer: ✅ True

Q8. Agile adoption changes

A) Identify Scrum Master
B) Iterative delivery
C) Remove documentation
D) Test automation

Answer: ✅ A, B and D

Q9. Choose INCORRECT statements

A) Longer sprint if priorities change often
B) PO decides sprint length
C) Sprint duration should remain constant
D) Shorter sprints give faster feedback

Answer: ✅ A and B

Q10. Potentially shippable increment

A) Product Backlog
B) Architecture document
C) Prototype implementation
D) Test plan

Answer: ✅ Prototype Implementation

Q11. Final decision on release scope & date

A) Team
B) Scrum Master
C) Product Owner
D) CEO

Answer: ✅ Product Owner

Q12. Estimation issue

A) Estimation done early
B) All team not involved
C) External review needed
D) Use story points instead of man-days

Answer: ✅ B and D

Q13. Capacity calculation
Team: 8 members
10 days, 6 hrs/day
1 member vacation (5 days)
2 members training (2.5 days each)

Answer: ✅ 420 hours

Q14. Velocity calculation
U1 = 3 (done)
U2 = 3 (done)
U3 = 5 (incomplete)

Answer: ✅ 6

Q15. FALSE statement about backlog prioritization

A) Continuous prioritization
B) Priority fixed in sprint
C) Incomplete story keeps same priority
D) PO finalizes priority

Answer: ✅ Incomplete story keeps same priority

Q16. Story points calculation
Velocity = 40
22 weeks → 11 sprints
1 pre-release sprint
25% buffer

Answer: ✅ 320

Q17. Daily Scrum issues

A) Bad timing
B) Long discussions
C) 15 min meeting
D) Status updates

Answer: ✅ A and B

Q18. Correct statement about user stories

A) 3 C’s (Card, Conversation, Confirmation)
B) IEEE format
C) Takes multiple sprints
D) Uses function points

Answer: ✅ 3 C’s

Q19. NOT focus of retrospective

A) Continue
B) Start
C) Product features
D) Stop

Answer: ✅ Product features

Q20. Agile vs Waterfall benefits

A) Easy changes
B) Fixed requirements
C) Early testing
D) Big bang delivery

Answer: ✅ A and C
